 fail-open delivery). Credential-free verified-fake Cloud/DC via _coordinator_harness.py (frozen clock, no network). 47 passed.\nAC3 (route census + poison, no reachable removed fallback): test_coordinator_route_census.py green (route_for('create')=='coordinator'; legacy path poisoned).\nAC4 (ADR 0103 ownership/taxonomy/fuse/containment/deltas/cutover/no-delete rollback): finalized Proposed->Accepted with the failure-taxonomy (11->5 buckets), fuse/containment, and no-remote-delete rollback sections.\nAC5 (architecture/operator docs: versioned outcomes + future adapter obligations): docs/architecture.md RP-03 planner->coordinator->adapter section.\nAC6 (ADR numbering + doc index + architecture links): tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py + tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py green.\n\nTDD: behavioral tests authored held-out (a background agent authored the E2E suite from the venue-cutover wiring; edge/E2E withheld from it), validated independently, teeth-verified by mutation (replay_safety_for commit_unknown->safe made s8/s9 RED; removing the fuse is_fuse_eligible guard made s4 RED; both restored). No production code changed (validates merged S1-S4).\n\nCI note: ps1 hit a Verified-1 from an import-mode collision (engine-tier tests mislocated in the interface-parity tier poisoned sys.modules['rebar_reconciler'], breaking rebar_reconciler.classify.* collection). Fixed by relocating the suite to the unit engine tier (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/) next to the reused venue-cutover harness, removing the sys.path hack; ps2 passed both gates and merged. file_impact + verify_commands updated to the relocated paths.","timestamp":1787746400795401001}],"created_at":1787028501753848001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f9f4ea38-11b5-4cf4-83b6-d356f3a444f9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b81b-8671-3c61-488f"},{"link_uuid":"8d733016-b7a8-4732-b77a-16a8784c9b6c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0f5d-2a24-91d2-4148"},{"link_uuid":"539f5a3b-60d3-4d83-b429-f5b720fd3bbd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d303-ae8b-14fa-422b"},{"link_uuid":"40a20fd1-0451-469b-b4ee-5f23b7e31c6a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"efe9-c8d2-a111-49f7"}],"description":"## Context\nContract removal is complete only when the entire planner/coordinator/adapter path passes portable end-to-end scenarios and the architecture, operator behavior, future adapter obligations, and rollback are durable.\n\n## Outcome\nRun credential-free verified-fake Cloud/DC passes over the complete taxonomy, finalize ADR 0103 and architecture/operator docs, and prove no removed production path is reachable.\n\n## Plan\n1. Build end-to-end fake Cloud/DC passes covering mixed success, transient recovery, long-delay deferral, permanent ticket failure, auth/provider stop, fuse open/reset, label-first create, restart, partial outcome, and delivery failure.\n2. Run the route census and runtime poison checks with the end-to-end suite. Keep bounded live probes optional operator evidence rather than a portable gate.\n3. Finalize ADR 0103 with retry ownership, failure taxonomy, fuse, containment, intentional deltas, expand/contract cutover, and rollback.\n4. Document planner -> coordinator -> adapter dependency direction, versioned output, operations guidance, and future adapter atomic-operation/retry obligations.\n5. Verify rollback re-observes remote state and never deletes successful Jira work.\n\n## Testing\nThe interface suite uses no external credentials and runs in every supported local/CI environment. ADR/doc index and route-census tests are mandatory.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Portable fake Cloud/DC suites cover every named outcome, fuse, create, restart, partial, and delivery scenario.\n- [x] End-to-end tests require no external credential or CI-provider-specific trigger.\n- [x] Route census and poison tests find no reachable removed fallback.\n- [x] ADR 0103 records ownership, taxonomy, fuse, containment, intentional deltas, cutover, and no-delete rollback.\n- [x] Architecture/operator docs define versioned outcomes and future adapter obligations.\n- [x] ADR numbering, documentation index, and architecture links pass.\n\n## Out of scope\nOptional live probes do not gate completion.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_reconciler_coordinator.py","reason":"Portable credential-free Cloud/DC end-to-end coordinator validation (scenarios 1-6 + venue parity), engine tier alongside the reused venue-cutover harness."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_reconciler_coordinator_taxonomy.py","reason":"Create/restart/partial/delivery taxonomy scenarios 7-10."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/_coordinator_harness.py","reason":"Shared credential-free coordinator test harness reusing the venue-cutover verified-fake wiring."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py","reason":"Final route census and poison checks (already proves AC3/AC6 behaviorally)."},{"path":"docs/adr/0103-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Finalize retry, taxonomy, fuse, containment, cutover, and rollback decisions."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"Document planner/coordinator/adapter dependency direction and adapter obligations."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0f5d-2a24-91d2-4148"],["depends_on","b81b-8671-3c61-488f"],["parent","3350-90b1-2651-4c50"],["relates_to","d303-ae8b-14fa-422b"],["relates_to","efe9-c8d2-a111-49f7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3350-90b1-2651-4c50","parent_status_uuid":"0b104a61-cc78-42c2-9fea-73eff74c4df9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["rp03","coordinator","adr","tdd"],"ticket_id":"a735-052e-8eca-4aeb","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S5 T